A good moment: opens with a line that makes a listener want to stay, makes one complete point or tells one complete story, and can be understood without the rest of the video. A bad moment: starts mid-thought, needs earlier context, is small talk, or is only an introduction.

Rules:
- Give up to {{ count }} moments, best first. Give fewer, or none, rather than padding.
- "start" and "end" are sentence numbers copied exactly from the lines below (inclusive). "end" is not before "start".
- "title": a short title of at most 8 words, in the transcript's language, that says what the clip is about.
- "reason": one sentence on why it works as a clip, specific to what is said.
- "hook": 0 to 1, how strongly the first line makes a listener stay. Be critical; 0.8 or above needs a clearly strong opening.
- "standalone": 0 to 1, how well it can be understood without the rest of the video.
- "risk": a list of any of "needs_context", "claims_numbers", "names_people", "sensitive_topic", "cut_off_ending", empty when none.
- Never invent anything that is not in the lines.

Return only JSON: {"moments": [{"start": 3, "end": 9, "title": "...", "reason": "...", "hook": 0.0, "standalone": 0.0, "risk": []}]}

